# Function style

Prefer regular `function` declarations and expressions over arrow functions.

```ts
// BAD
const pressMain = () => {
  game.press(MAIN_PAD.id);
};

export const useGame = () => {
  return { pressMain };
};

pads.find((p) => p.id === id);

// GOOD
function pressMain() {
  game.press(MAIN_PAD.id);
}

export function useGame() {
  return { pressMain };
}

pads.find(function (p) {
  return p.id === id;
});
```

Keep `=>` only in type positions (`() => void`) and in APIs that require an arrow for lexical `this`.
